  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z-3=\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the paraboloid, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-3 & =\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =\\frac{25}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-3 & =5-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ z-8 & =-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-4(z-8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis gives us the equation of the parabola in $yz$-plane.",
